docs/HUNCHLANE_BUSINESS_PLAN.md:31:> Create a 12-month business plan for Hunchlane, a beginner-friendly idea research app. Use USD. Clearly label every volume, price and cost as an unvalidated assumption. Test a future $5 pack containing one report and one refinement. Assume total variable cost $1.60 per paid pack, fixed costs $40/month, month-one paid volume 20 packs, 10% monthly volume growth and starting capital $200. Add a separate one-time $23 pilot research cost. Show monthly revenue, variable costs, gross profit, fixed costs, operating profit and cash. Show break-even volume and runway where cash becomes negative. Compare conservative volume 12 packs/month with 5% growth, base volume 20 with 10% growth, and optimistic volume 28 with 12.5% growth. Keep temporary sponsor grants separate from sustainable costs. Add a no-growth case and a sensitivity case where research costs double. Do not claim market demand, customer traction or guaranteed profit. Ask for any missing assumptions needed to complete a coherent model.
docs/HUNCHLANE_BUSINESS_PLAN.md:35:- Contribution per paid pack: $5 − $1.60 = $3.40.
docs/HUNCHLANE_BUSINESS_PLAN.md:36:- Operating break-even: ceil($40 ÷ $3.40) = 12 paid packs/month, before the one-time pilot cost and taxes.
docs/HUNCHLANE_BUSINESS_PLAN.md:39:- Optimistic month 1: revenue $140; variable cost $44.80; operating profit $55.20; ending cash $232.20 after the pilot cost.
docs/HUNCHLANE_BUSINESS_PLAN.md:55:> Price per paid pack = $5; each pack contains one report and one refinement. Research cost hypothesis = $1.15/paid pack; payment and support = $0.45/paid pack; total variable cost = $1.60. Fixed costs = $40/month. Opening cash = $200, a modeling assumption. One-time free pilot = 20 packs in month 1, costing 20 × research cost ($23 in normal cases). Paid pack sales and their cash receipts occur in the same month. Pay all costs in the same month. Assume no debt, capex, inventory, receivables, payables, owner salary or distributions; show pre-tax results and explicitly exclude tax and founder labor from viability conclusions. No recurring free allowance beyond the one-time pilot. No sponsor grants enter cash or recurring cost calculations.
docs/HUNCHLANE_BUSINESS_PLAN.md:57:> Use six scenarios: Conservative starts at 12 paid packs and grows 5% monthly; Base starts at 20 and grows 10%; Optimistic starts at 28 and grows 12.5%; No growth stays at 20; Double research cost uses Base volume/growth with research cost $2.30, total variable cost $2.75, and one-time pilot cost $46; No sales sells zero packs with normal costs and a $23 pilot. For month m use units = ROUND(initial_units × (1 + growth)^(m − 1), 0), always from the unrounded starting-volume formula, not from the previous rounded month. Round currency to cents. Revenue = units × price; variable costs = units × total variable cost; contribution = revenue − variable costs; operating profit before pilot = contribution − fixed costs; net cash movement = operating profit − pilot cost in month 1; ending cash = opening cash + cumulative net cash movement. Keep pilot costs separately visible to avoid double-counting them.
